{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested at exact dd34b5e287d3106a83f90ec272d48debf2adf11d, all 105 changed paths versus corrected S5 b070ffbf, S6 results note first. Reviewed in a separate detached checkout: npm ci, npm ci --prefix experiments/pds, npm run check (0), npm run test:archive (9/9), npm test (276/276, 0 skipped), then npm run spike:acceptance, which passed all 13 commands and reproduced the measurements in the same range: 10,000-entry confirmed append p50 15.5 s against the retained 16.5 s, Node full replay 7.3 s against 7.9 s, browser replay and transfer 15.1 s against 15.1 s, summed Chromium RSS 1308 MiB against 1319 MiB. All sourceHashes in the 13 retained experiments files and in agent-authored/verification.json match HEAD; all 13 acceptance log hashes match their logs; the nearest-rank p50 and p95 recompute exactly from the nine raw samples at each size; no credentials, tokens or private keys appear in evidence, transcripts, docs or notes; src/ carries no domain vocabulary; the retained evolved, chart and agent archives replay at this head and the pre-S5 agent archive is refused for its older runtime, so the two agent runs are genuinely separated; the agent transcript uses only documented adapter operations.\n\nThree required changes, plus the inherited S5 defect.\n\nFirst, a trust-boundary defect at archive import. A genesis is unsigned: Anchor.from checks only that the genesis matches its CID, so anyone can mint a genesis for an existing app DID with their own sequencer and activation keys. importArchive (src/archive/archive.ts line 77) checks the genesis against an invitation only when an expected pin is supplied, and the browser imports with no pin (src/browser/main.ts line 315), then replaces the sidebar entry for that app DID with the archive's genesis (line 318). Reproduced: an archive forged from the evolved app's DID with attacker keys and an empty history imports successfully unpinned and is refused only when pinned. That is an automatic trust reset, which the plan's sketch E forbids (\"a conflicting genesis or signature is shown as a verification problem with no automatic trust reset\") and which docs/archives.md line 18 does not describe. Fix: when the device already holds an invitation for that app DID, pass it as expected and surface a conflict as a verification problem rather than replacing it; pin a test for the conflicting-genesis import.\n\nSecond, the worker watchdog cancels every long local replay, export and import at 15 seconds. src/browser/evaluator.ts line 15 adds a timeoutMs parameter and line 17 still hard-codes 15000, so the 120000 passed for sync, compare, export and import is ignored. The retained browser measurement of 15.1 seconds at 10,000 entries was taken by driving the worker directly; through the shipped shell that replay would be cancelled with \"Evaluation timed out\". docs/archives.md says long local replay has a visible working message and can be cancelled, which implies it can also finish. Fix the one line and pin it with a test that a call given a longer budget survives past 15 seconds, or that the timer uses the argument.\n\nThird, the plan gate says a failed gate stays failed with its exact reproduction, but scripts/acceptance.ts lines 27 to 33 copy the generated report and logs into experiments only when every command passed, the recommendation is a fixed string, and scripts/report.ts would still emit a passing note from the prior retained report if source hashes are unchanged. The retained machine-readable report therefore cannot show a failure. Record the failing run's report and logs in the retained location, or refuse to leave a stale pass standing.\n\nInherited: this head contains S5 b070ffbf, whose sync path still drops a signed closure over the 512 KiB CAR bound while the host judges it invalid_activation (verdict d16125c3). S6 neither fixes nor worsens it; rebase onto the corrected S5 once it lands.\n\nNon-blocking. experiments/feasibility.json and agent-authored/verification.json were rewritten by later reruns after the recorded acceptance run, so they are not the outputs of the 13 recorded commands although their source hashes match HEAD. The 13 commands omit npm ci and add four not in the plan's section 8 list; say so rather than \"all recorded commands\". The 51 unchanged host and build hashes are two committed files captured by the parent, so the assertion cannot fail as retained, and the five built-shell hashes are unverifiable because the build is not committed. The rebuild comparison covers state, definition, outcomes and frontier against the host cache but the host persists no retry index, so the retry comparison is rebuild against import only. The import.csv placed in the chart fixture is never read; the rows come from four signed actions. The cancellation test swallows the export message so the worker never starts; it pins the UI path and outbox retention, not termination of in-flight work. offlineServiceWorker, responsivenessClickObserved and hostAndBuildUnchanged are labels written after their asserts. Several archive guards are unpinned: the entry, candidate and inventory bounds, unknown-field refusals, source root versus genesis, candidate CAR identity, the 48 MiB limit, invalid UTF-8, the licenses and replay-text equality, and the CLI replay pinned-invitation mismatch. The licenses and replay-text equality checks make an archive from an identical runtime CID with different installed license texts unimportable; runtime identity should decide, not notice text.\n\nArchitecture: a new archive layer over the runtime and protocol contracts, with the shell gaining a service worker, import and export; docs/archives.md documents it. Security: the unpinned import is an authority defect at the archive boundary; keys are otherwise excluded by construction, imports verify runtime, signatures, inventory and deterministic replay, and exports carry no credentials. Simplification: drop the notice and replay-text equality from import. The measured recommendation to revise complete-prefix serving before long-lived histories is supported by the raw samples and by my rerun. Nothing here adopts the plan-review recommendations.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:fa8d62ed900d7697380a68652abb3e45d950a677#git:sha1:6b9e5c10a2859a4e53a18f32b20dbe25858f31d3","head":"dd34b5e287d3106a83f90ec272d48debf2adf11d","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:fa8d62ed900d7697380a68652abb3e45d950a677#git:sha1:a6df2c50e05145f10805b036a020294bfb6de7f1\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:fa8d62ed900d7697380a68652abb3e45d950a677#git:sha1:89e0dd0d1dd91a25eb1294f2ed561b60f045cf86","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}